Theme colors are now stored as Color Groups and Block Themes, in the JSON registry fields `color_groups` and `block_themes`, replacing the per-color fields such as `primary_color_light` and `font_family_primary`. Existing themes keep their colors, and the upgrade step to profile version 1002 converts them. Profiles that still set the old fields on `ISCVLTThemeDefinition` keep installing, including on the `default` theme, where their colors replace the shipped palette. `font_family_secondary` and the event, file and image colors are still stored and served as before. The Themes control panel serves `ISCVLTThemeSchema`, which has only the new fields, and rejects malformed Color Groups or Block Themes with a `400` instead of deleting the custom ones. Color Group ids use letters, digits and underscores. @Humanaice @ericof
